1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,420
You ever sit there at night thinking, man... I really need to get my whole life together?

2
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:05,140
Tonight?

3
00:00:05,360 --> 00:00:06,880
Well... eventually.

4
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:11,710
Good. Because tonight you're exhausted, overwhelmed, and being a little dramatic.

5
00:00:11,930 --> 00:00:12,630
A little?

6
00:00:12,850 --> 00:00:14,130
I'm being supportive.

7
00:00:14,350 --> 00:00:21,770
I think that's where people get stuck. They start thinking about forever. Forever sober. Forever disciplined. Never screwing up again.

8
00:00:21,990 --> 00:00:24,130
Forever is huge. Try today.

9
00:00:24,350 --> 00:00:25,150
Just today?

10
00:00:25,370 --> 00:00:30,150
Today is plenty. What do you need to do before you go to sleep without making your life worse?

11
00:00:30,370 --> 00:00:32,210
Wanting a better life matters.

12
00:00:32,430 --> 00:00:37,160
Absolutely. But your actions eventually need to find out about this wonderful new plan.

13
00:00:37,380 --> 00:00:42,550
So make the call. Go home when you know you should go home. Show up tomorrow. Tell the truth.

14
00:00:42,770 --> 00:00:45,350
Desire gets you pointed in the right direction.

15
00:00:45,570 --> 00:00:47,310
And your feet still have to move.

16
00:00:47,530 --> 00:00:51,300
One thing I've learned is that things get dangerous when you disappear into your own head.

17
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:58,440
Especially when your brain starts saying, don't tell anybody. I can handle this myself. How'd that strategy work last time?

18
00:00:58,660 --> 00:01:00,320
Rude. Accurate, though.

19
00:01:00,540 --> 00:01:05,360
Call somebody before you do the thing you already know you're going to regret. Not afterward.

20
00:01:05,580 --> 00:01:08,400
And sometimes you have to admit you can't control everything.

21
00:01:08,620 --> 00:01:10,130
He hates this section.

22
00:01:10,350 --> 00:01:11,250
I really do.

23
00:01:11,470 --> 00:01:12,110
I know.

24
00:01:12,330 --> 00:01:21,630
You don't have to have every spiritual answer figured out. Call it God. Faith. Purpose. Your Higher Power. Something bigger than whatever emotion happens to be screaming the loudest right now.

25
00:01:21,850 --> 00:01:24,160
Because not every feeling deserves a vote.

26
00:01:24,380 --> 00:01:29,320
Ask for enough direction to do the next right thing. That's enough for today.

27
00:01:29,540 --> 00:01:39,130
At the end of the day, take a minute and be honest with yourself. What did I do right? Where was I full of crap? Did I hurt somebody? Is there something I need to apologize for or make right?

28
00:01:39,350 --> 00:01:45,300
And then fix what you can. Don't turn self-reflection into a three-hour meeting about how terrible you are.

29
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:46,450
Be accountable.

30
00:01:46,670 --> 00:01:47,630
Not cruel.

31
00:01:47,850 --> 00:01:49,670
You're still going to have bad days.

32
00:01:49,890 --> 00:01:54,320
You'll get angry. Tired. Lonely. Somebody will get on your last nerve.

33
00:01:54,540 --> 00:01:56,100
You might even screw something up.

34
00:01:56,320 --> 00:02:01,230
But one bad decision does not require another one. A bad day doesn't need a sequel.

35
00:02:01,450 --> 00:02:05,210
Get honest. Reach out. Correct course. And keep moving.

36
00:02:05,430 --> 00:02:10,370
Eventually something else happens. You stop spending every waking minute thinking about your own problems.

37
00:02:10,590 --> 00:02:13,060
Which is healthy, because that room gets crowded.

38
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:18,180
You help somebody. You check on somebody. You encourage the person who's a few steps behind you.

39
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:23,870
And suddenly your worst years aren't completely wasted. They taught you something another person might need.

40
00:02:24,090 --> 00:02:31,390
That's what a comeback usually looks like. Not some giant movie moment. You get through today differently. Then tomorrow. Then another day.

41
00:02:31,610 --> 00:02:34,450
And after a while, you start collecting evidence.

42
00:02:34,670 --> 00:02:35,830
Evidence of what?

43
00:02:36,050 --> 00:02:41,940
That maybe you're not that old version of yourself anymore. You're just still used to talking about yourself like you are.

44
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:44,660
So no. You don't need a whole new life tonight.

45
00:02:44,880 --> 00:02:46,200
You need some honesty.

46
00:02:46,420 --> 00:02:47,640
Some willingness.

47
00:02:47,860 --> 00:02:49,100
People you can call.

48
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:50,970
Something bigger than yourself.

49
00:02:51,190 --> 00:02:52,850
And one decent decision.

50
00:02:53,070 --> 00:02:53,720
Today.

51
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:59,240
Of course, tomorrow morning you're probably going to wake up and feel absolutely zero motivation.

52
00:02:59,460 --> 00:03:02,120
Can I enjoy this victory for like ten seconds?

53
00:03:02,340 --> 00:03:02,970
Nope.
